---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Faq from '../../../components/Faq.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, localePath } from '../../../lib/url';

const toolPath = '/en/tools/job-task-analysis-tracker/';
const productPath = `${localePath('en', 'worksite-skills-ledger')}?utm_source=funnytools&utm_medium=owned&utm_campaign=product011_launch&utm_content=free_tool`;
const faqItems = [{ q: 'What does this free tracker store?', a: 'It temporarily summarizes the anonymous task steps you enter in this browser page. It does not create a participant profile or upload the fields.' }, { q: 'Does NOT OBSERVED count as incorrect?', a: 'No. It is displayed separately and is excluded from the valid observed-step denominator.' }, { q: 'Does this make a professional recommendation?', a: 'No. The page is a descriptive worksheet, not a vocational assessment, placement tool, or employment decision system.' }];
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Free Job Task Analysis Tracker | FunnyTools" description="Enter anonymous task steps locally and review independence, prompt, quality, and support observations in a printable task snapshot." keywords={['job task analysis template', 'vocational task analysis', 'job coach task tracker', 'worksite independence tracker']} type="website" canonicalPath={toolPath} hasAlternates={false} ogImage={absoluteUrl('/assets/product-011/03-og.png')} ogImageAlt="Free Job Task Analysis Tracker" jsonLd={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Free Job Task Analysis Tracker', applicationCategory: 'EducationApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', description: 'A local browser worksheet for anonymous task-step observations.' }, { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: item.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a } })) }]} automaticAffiliate={false}>
  <article class="product-011-tool-page" data-tool-page="job-task-analysis-tracker"><div class="wrap"><Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: localePath('en') }, { label: 'Tools', href: localePath('en', 'tools') }, { label: 'Free Job Task Analysis Tracker' }]} /></div><section class="wrap tool-011-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">FREE LOCAL BROWSER TOOL</p><h1>Free Job Task Analysis Tracker</h1><p class="lead">Enter a few anonymous task steps and review what was recorded across independence, prompts, supports, quality, and time.</p></div><div class="tool-011-privacy"><strong>No data upload.</strong><span>Use a task label and worksite-neutral step descriptions. Do not enter a participant full name, employer name, or identifying notes.</span></div></section>
    <section class="wrap tool-011-form-section"><form id="job-task-form"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">TASK ANALYSIS</p><h2>What did you observe?</h2></div><button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="add-step">ADD STEP</button></div><div class="field"><label for="task-label">Task label</label><input id="task-label" maxlength="120" placeholder="Stock Shelves"></div><div id="task-rows" class="tool-011-rows"></div><p id="form-error" class="safety-note" hidden></p><button class="btn go" type="submit">BUILD TASK SNAPSHOT</button></form></section>
    <section id="results" class="wrap tool-011-results" hidden aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SUMMARY</p><h2 id="results-title">Recorded task snapshot</h2></div><button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="print-result">PRINT SNAPSHOT</button></div><div id="result-summary" class="tool-011-summary"></div><div id="result-table" class="table-wrap"></div><div class="tool-011-bridge"><strong>Tracking more than one task or worksite?</strong><span>Worksite Skills Ledger adds participants, worksites, sessions, support trends, task time, quality, hours, generalization, reports, and backups.</span><a class="btn go" data-product-event="product_011_free_to_paid_click" data-placement="free_tool_result" data-destination="product_page" href={productPath}>TRACK THE FULL WORK EXPERIENCE — $29</a></div><p class="safety-note">This snapshot describes only the anonymous rows entered on this page. It does not determine ability, work capacity, placement, eligibility, effectiveness, or professional recommendations.</p></section>
    <section class="wrap tool-011-notes"><h2>Use the tracker as a conversation starter</h2><p>A blank or unobserved step means it was not entered as observed in this worksheet. It does not establish inability or a negative work conclusion. Keep the source context and professional interpretation in the record system approved by your organization.</p><h2>How to read the snapshot</h2><p>Start with the task label, then enter one observable action per row. Choose the independence status that matches the observation, and add a prompt, support, quality label, or minutes only when that detail is useful and known. Independent percentage uses only valid observed steps: independent, prompted, or not completed. NOT OBSERVED remains visible but is excluded from that denominator. Prompt and support counts show distinct labels entered on this page; they are not a progress score. The worksheet does not compare a person with a norm, a job requirement, or another participant. Repeat the same task only when the observation context is meaningful, and preserve the surrounding notes in an approved record system.</p><h2>A simple observation routine</h2><p>Before starting, agree on the task label and decide what counts as one observable step for this particular session. Short, concrete steps are easier to review than a broad label such as “did the job.” For example, a team might separate locating supplies, carrying the cart, checking the shelf label, placing an item, and returning unused materials. The tracker does not decide whether those steps are appropriate; it gives the observer a place to record the team’s own definition. During the observation, select one independence status for each entered step. Add a prompt or support only when it was actually used or when the team intentionally records that category as not coded. Add minutes when the timing method is clear. A missing optional field is different from a negative result.</p><p>After building the snapshot, read the table from top to bottom and check whether the recorded labels match what the observer intended. A high independent percentage can coexist with a support label because the team may be tracking a support that was available, offered, or used in a particular way. A low percentage can reflect the task, context, instruction, fatigue, equipment, timing, or an incomplete observation; the worksheet cannot identify the cause. Use the print action when a paper discussion is useful, and keep the surrounding context with the snapshot. If more than one observer is involved, agree on labels and observation conditions before comparing separate records. Do not treat this small worksheet as a replacement for the documentation, consent, supervision, accessibility, or data-governance process required by your organization.</p><h2>When a fuller ledger is useful</h2><p>This free page is intentionally narrow: it gives you a local task-step snapshot with a few descriptive fields. A fuller workflow may be useful when your team needs multiple participant codes, worksite codes, reusable task libraries, session history, hours, task time, quality labels, support trends, generalization matrices, JSON backup, CSV export, and printable reports. Worksite Skills Ledger keeps those dimensions organized in a local-first buyer app without requiring an account or subscription for the core experience. It still does not prescribe a work standard, rank people, predict employment, or make a hiring, placement, eligibility, medical, disability, or vocational decision. The decision about whether a fuller record is appropriate belongs to the responsible team.</p><h2>Privacy and boundary reminders</h2><p>Do not enter full names, birth dates, contact details, diagnoses, employee numbers, employer names, or identifying free-text notes. This page does not upload the fields to FunnyTools analytics, but browser-local processing is not a substitute for device security or organizational retention rules. Clear the page when the session is complete if the device is shared, and follow your organization’s approved retention and deletion process. If a record must be retained, use the organization’s controlled system rather than treating this public worksheet as the authoritative record.</p></section><div class="wrap"><Faq lang="en" items={faqItems} emitJsonLd={false} /></div></article>
  <script is:inline>
    (() => { const rowsElement = document.querySelector('#task-rows'); const form = document.querySelector('#job-task-form'); const results = document.querySelector('#results'); const errorElement = document.querySelector('#form-error'); const productId = 'PRODUCT-011'; const toolId = 'job-task-analysis-tracker'; const track = (name, params = {}) => window.__ft_track?.(name, params); const send = (name, params = {}) => track(name, params); let toolStarted = false; const markToolStarted = (controlType) => { if (toolStarted) return; toolStarted = true; send('tool_started', { control_type: controlType }); send('tool_use_started', { control_type: controlType }); }; let rows = [{ step: '', independence: 'NOT OBSERVED', prompt: '', support: '', quality: 'NOT RATED', minutes: '' }]; const promptLevels = ['Independent', 'Visual Cue', 'Gesture', 'Indirect Verbal', 'Direct Verbal', 'Model', 'Partial Physical', 'Full Physical', 'Other']; const supports = ['Visual cue', 'Task checklist', 'Verbal reminder', 'Model', 'Environmental setup', 'Scheduled break', 'Other']; const quality = ['NOT RATED', 'NEEDS REWORK', 'PARTIALLY MEETS USER-DEFINED EXPECTATION', 'MEETS USER-DEFINED EXPECTATION', 'EXCEEDS USER-DEFINED EXPECTATION']; const esc = (value) => String(value ?? '').replace(/[&<>"']/g, (char) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' }[char])); const optionList = (values, selected, blank) => `${blank !== undefined ? `<option value="">${blank}</option>` : ''}${values.map((value) => `<option${value === selected ? ' selected' : ''}>${esc(value)}</option>`).join('')}`; const render = () => { rowsElement.innerHTML = rows.map((row, index) => `<div class="tool-011-row"><strong>${index + 1}</strong><label>Step<input data-key="step" data-index="${index}" value="${esc(row.step)}" placeholder="Identify shelf section"></label><label>Independence<select data-key="independence" data-index="${index}">${optionList(['INDEPENDENT', 'PROMPTED', 'NOT COMPLETED', 'NOT OBSERVED'], row.independence)}</select></label><label>Prompt<select data-key="prompt" data-index="${index}">${optionList(promptLevels, row.prompt, 'Not coded')}</select></label><label>Support<select data-key="support" data-index="${index}">${optionList(supports, row.support, 'Not coded')}</select></label><label>Quality<select data-key="quality" data-index="${index}">${optionList(quality, row.quality)}</select></label><label>Minutes<input data-key="minutes" data-index="${index}" type="number" min="0" step="0.25" value="${esc(row.minutes)}"></label></div>`).join(''); }; const collect = () => { document.querySelectorAll('[data-index]').forEach((el) => { rows[Number(el.dataset.index)][el.dataset.key] = el.value; }); return rows; }; const summary = (taskLabel, data) => { const valid = data.filter((row) => ['INDEPENDENT', 'PROMPTED', 'NOT COMPLETED'].includes(row.independence)); const independent = valid.filter((row) => row.independence === 'INDEPENDENT').length; const observed = data.filter((row) => row.independence !== 'NOT OBSERVED').length; const supportsCount = new Set(data.map((row) => row.support).filter(Boolean)).size; const promptsCount = new Set(data.map((row) => row.prompt).filter(Boolean)).size; return `<div><small>Task</small><strong>${esc(taskLabel || 'User-defined task')}</strong></div><div><small>Valid observed steps</small><strong>${valid.length} / ${data.length}</strong></div><div><small>Independent</small><strong>${valid.length ? Math.round(independent / valid.length * 100) : '—'}%</strong></div><div><small>Prompt labels</small><strong>${promptsCount}</strong></div><div><small>Support labels</small><strong>${supportsCount}</strong></div><div><small>Not observed</small><strong>${data.length - observed}</strong></div>`; }; const renderResult = (taskLabel, data) => { document.querySelector('#result-summary').innerHTML = summary(taskLabel, data); document.querySelector('#result-table').innerHTML = `<table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Independence</th><th>Prompt</th><th>Support</th><th>Quality</th><th>Minutes</th></tr></thead><tbody>${data.map((row) => `<tr><td>${esc(row.step || 'Unlabelled step')}</td><td>${esc(row.independence)}</td><td>${esc(row.prompt || '—')}</td><td>${esc(row.support || '—')}</td><td>${esc(row.quality)}</td><td>${esc(row.minutes || '—')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`; results.hidden = false; results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); send('tool_completed'); send('tool_use_completed'); track('product_011_free_tool_complete', { product_id: productId, tool_id: toolId }); }; document.querySelector('#add-step').addEventListener('click', () => { collect(); if (rows.length >= 15) return; rows.push({ step: '', independence: 'NOT OBSERVED', prompt: '', support: '', quality: 'NOT RATED', minutes: '' }); render(); send('tool_action', { action_name: 'add_step' }); }); rowsElement.addEventListener('input', () => { collect(); markToolStarted('input'); }); rowsElement.addEventListener('change', () => collect()); form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => { event.preventDefault(); collect(); errorElement.hidden = true; const taskLabel = document.querySelector('#task-label').value.trim(); const complete = rows.filter((row) => row.step.trim()); if (!complete.length) { errorElement.textContent = 'Add at least one task step.'; errorElement.hidden = false; send('tool_error', { error_type: 'validation' }); return; } renderResult(taskLabel, complete); send('tool_action', { action_name: 'build_task_snapshot' }); }); document.querySelector('#print-result').addEventListener('click', () => { send('result_action', { action_name: 'print' }); send('file_download', { download_action: 'print_snapshot' }); window.print(); }); document.querySelectorAll('[data-product-event]').forEach((link) => link.addEventListener('click', () => track(link.dataset.productEvent, { product_id: productId, tool_id: toolId, placement: link.dataset.placement, destination: link.dataset.destination }))); render(); send('tool_view'); track('product_011_free_tool_view', { product_id: productId, tool_id: toolId }); })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .product-011-tool-page{--tool-ink:#102b3b;--tool-teal:#1d7c83;--tool-mint:#dcefe9;--tool-muted:#5d7380}.tool-011-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(260px,.6fr);gap:30px;align-items:end;padding:20px 0 34px}.tool-011-hero h1{color:var(--tool-ink);font-size:clamp(2.3rem,5vw,4.8rem);letter-spacing:-.055em;line-height:.98;margin:12px 0 18px}.tool-011-hero .lead{color:var(--tool-muted);font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:650px}.tool-011-privacy{padding:18px;border-left:4px solid var(--tool-teal);background:var(--tool-mint);border-radius:10px;color:var(--tool-ink)}.tool-011-privacy strong,.tool-011-privacy span{display:block}.tool-011-privacy span{margin-top:7px;color:var(--tool-muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.55}.tool-011-form-section,.tool-011-results{padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;background:var(--card);box-shadow:var(--shadow-soft);margin-top:22px}.tool-011-rows{display:grid;gap:12px;margin:18px 0}.tool-011-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:32px minmax(160px,1.4fr) repeat(5,minmax(105px,1fr));gap:9px;align-items:end;padding:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:#fbfdfd}.tool-011-row>strong{width:28px;height:28px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--tool-teal);border-radius:50%;color:#fff}.tool-011-row label{display:grid;gap:5px;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:750;color:var(--tool-ink)}.tool-011-row input,.tool-011-row select{min-height:38px;padding:8px;font-size:.78rem}.tool-011-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:10px;margin:20px 0}.tool-011-summary>div{padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}.tool-011-summary small,.tool-011-summary strong{display:block}.tool-011-summary small{color:var(--tool-muted)}.tool-011-summary strong{margin-top:5px;color:var(--tool-ink)}.tool-011-bridge{display:grid;gap:8px;margin-top:22px;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;background:var(--tool-mint)}.tool-011-bridge span{color:var(--tool-muted)}.tool-011-notes{max-width:900px;padding:55px 0}.tool-011-notes p{color:var(--tool-muted);line-height:1.7}.tool-011-tool-page .eyebrow{color:var(--tool-teal);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.13em}.tool-011-tool-page .table-wrap table{min-width:700px}@media(max-width:900px){.tool-011-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tool-011-row{grid-template-columns:32px minmax(0,1fr) repeat(2,minmax(120px,1fr))}.tool-011-row label:nth-last-child(-n+3){grid-column:2 / -1}.tool-011-summary{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}}@media(max-width:600px){.tool-011-form-section,.tool-011-results{padding:17px}.tool-011-row{grid-template-columns:32px minmax(0,1fr)}.tool-011-row label,.tool-011-row label:nth-last-child(-n+3){grid-column:1 / -1}.tool-011-summary{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.tool-011-form-section .section-heading{display:block}.tool-011-form-section .section-heading .btn{margin-top:10px}}
</style>
